# |<----                Keep header under 72 characters               ---->|

# Explain WHY this change is being made and how it impacts Strapi v5 admin/server:
# |<----                  Wrap body lines at 100 chars                ---->|

# Footer (optional):
# Closes #123
# BREAKING CHANGE: <description of breaking change and migration steps>

# --- COMMIT CONVENTIONS (@vicacha-devs/strapi-v5-extensions) ---
# Allowed <type> values:
#   feat     - New plugin capability, Strapi v5 content-type, admin view, or REST route
#   fix      - Bug fix in admin UI, server controller/service, lifecycles, or types
#   docs     - Documentation and README updates
#   style    - Code formatting or Strapi Design System v2 styling adjustments
#   refactor - Refactoring code (e.g., splitting files to stay < 500 lines)
#   perf     - Query, caching, or bundle performance improvements
#   test     - Adding or updating Vitest unit tests (server or admin)
#   build    - @strapi/sdk-plugin build, tsup, Turborepo, or dependency updates
#   ci       - GitHub Actions, Changesets, or monorepo scripts
#   chore    - Routine maintenance tasks
#   revert   - Revert a previous commit
#
# Allowed <scope> values (package/plugin name):
#   bookings, broadcasts, calendar, certificates, donations, events,
#   inbox, islam, media-feeds, resources, dashboard, eslint-config,
#   typescript-config, repo, deps
#
# Examples:
#   feat(bookings): add configurable capacity buffer to reservation service
#   fix(islam): handle leap-year Hijri date conversion edge case
#   refactor(donations): split campaign controller into modular handlers (<500 lines)
